hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15581","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, he said: Four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered. One of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah the Blessed and Exalted accepts the repentance of the servant before he dies by a day."
"15582","The second said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah the Blessed and Exalted accepts the repentance of the servant before he dies by half a day."
"15583","The third said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah the Blessed and Exalted accepts the repentance of the servant before he dies by a forenoon."
"15584","The fourth said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah accepts the repentance of the servant so long as his soul does not gargle."
